# The oldest Atelier version whose DATABASE this image's converge can migrate.
#
# THE SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for this release's upgrade floor. Read twice from
# here, never typed twice:
#
#   - baked into the image at /etc/atelier/upgrade-floor, where converge.sh
#     reads it and REFUSES to migrate an older site (before touching the DB);
#   - stamped onto the image as LABEL dev.atelier.upgrade.min-from by the release
#     workflow, where the manager reads it FROM THE REGISTRY WITHOUT PULLING to
#     plan a stepped upgrade (0.1.1 → 0.3.0 → 0.4.0) instead of a doomed one.
#
# WHEN TO RAISE IT. Raise it in the same commit as any change that makes a
# migration from older state impossible or unsafe — most concretely, when a
# release DELETES the code that a still-pending update needs. Uninstalling a
# module is the canonical case: the hook_update_N that uninstalls `ai` must be
# present in the image that runs it, so the release that DROPS those packages
# from composer.json can no longer perform the uninstall, and can only migrate
# sites that already did. Set the floor to the oldest release that carries that
# work, and every older install is routed through it automatically.
#
# Raising it is a promise the registry has to keep: the value MUST be a released
# version with a published :vX.Y.Z tag, because that tag is the waypoint the
# manager pulls. A floor naming an unreleased version strands every old install.
#
# Format: one bare X.Y.Z (no leading v), comments and blank lines ignored.
0.1.0
